WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:05.240
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.540
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:31.300
This is Galar’s
Shoot City Station.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.060
It seems a train
has just arrived.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:44.820
Here at last!

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:45.990
Not quite yet.

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:47.330
We have to switch trains.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:48.610
I know.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:50.370
We’re going to
Lateral Town, right?

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:51.690
Which platform is it?

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:56.130
S-Sorry...

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:00.820
His ticket...

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:05.580
Hey, you!
You dropped this!

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:10.090
Hey!

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.470
Hey, look!
You dropped your ticket!

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:22.730
He went in here, right?

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:23.800
I guess...

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.550
Hey!

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:51.410
He’s not here.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:53.490
I wonder where he went.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:04.570
Platform 0, Lateral Town line,
is about to depart.

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:07.460
Passengers bound for this line
please enter the train now.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.740
You hear that?

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:10.610
It’s going to Lateral Town.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.160
Quick, Go!

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:16.800
The Ghost Train will now depart.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:16.100
Yeah!

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.350
Please refrain from running
to catch the train.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:23.360
Didn’t they call this the “Ghost Train”
or something just now?

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.970
Did they?

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:28.830
Well, as long as it’s going to
Lateral Town, it’s all good.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:32.920
Either way...
I better return this.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:35.920
Coach 1, huh...?

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:39.430
That means...
he’ll be in the passenger car at the very front.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:40.110
Yeah.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:41.550
‘Kay, you ready?

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:45.560
Ooh!

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:47.690
So fancy!

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:52.520
Is this one of those
luxury coaches?

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.500
What’s this thing?

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.040
Ow...

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:06.270
You okay, Satoshi?

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:07.950
Yeah.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:10.710
Come on, Sarunori,
you need to be more careful.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.090
Oh, no!

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:17.220
Phew,
it doesn’t look broken.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:20.870
It’s heavy!

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:23.080
What are you doing?

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:29.790
It— It won’t budge...

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:33.260
What’s wrong with this rock?
It’s way too heavy!

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.330
What should we do?

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:38.660
We can’t just leave it here...

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:46.320
Oh, well. We’ll get someone
to help put it back later.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.910
What was that?

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:52.600
Satoshi, are you all right?

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:54.130
Huh? Why’re you asking?

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:56.890
Never mind,
you seem fine.

00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:58.380
Well, let’s go.

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:00.430
Oh... Yeah.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.300
There’s something in there!

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.030
Huh? What’s up?

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.110
Didn’t you see that, Satoshi?!

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.970
What’re you so scared of?

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.660
You crack me up.

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:30.010
Huh?

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:35.340
What is it?

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:37.170
Even Pikachu looks scared.

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:40.830
What’s so strange
about me, huh?

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:41.860
Satoshi?

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:43.170
Come on, come on!

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:46.180
We need to get to
the next coach already!

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:48.300
Wait, stop!

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.530
And, bam!

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:56.870
What am I doing?

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.150
Sorry, Go...

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:02.380
What’s gotten into you
all of a sudden?

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:07.570
I think...

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.730
...there’s something
wrong with me...

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:14.580
Who are these guys?

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:19.870
Fuwante! Balloon Pokémon!
Ghost/Flying type!

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:24.090
It tugs on the hands of children
to drag them away to the afterlife!

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:26.140
The afterlife?!

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:28.460
It’ll be bad news
if they catch us...

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:31.550
Hey, don’t come closer!

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:34.090
Hey... Hey...

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:36.490
Hey, you!

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:37.360
Satoshi?

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.980
So, what kind of
bad news, exactly?

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.860
I-I’m saying weird stuff again!

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:45.810
Hey! Hey, wait a sec!

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:46.820
Stop! Stop!

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:48.590
This is such a laugh! I’m howling!

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.590
Cut it out!

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:50.000
Come, now!

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:53.690
If the Fuwante catch you,
off to the afterlife you’ll...

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:57.920
Go!

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:00.280
Nooo!

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:11.520
Huh? This doesn’t look like
the afterlife...

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:16.810
While it may tug on the hands of children,
sometimes the children pull it around instead!

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:19.560
You have to be kidding me...

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:22.310
You’re a <i>riot!</i>

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:25.070
I shoulda taken a photo of you!

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:28.410
What am I saying?
I’m being so mean...

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:31.620
Hey, Satoshi...
Don’t you think you’ve been acting weird?

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:32.530
I really have!

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:33.330
You think so?

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:36.700
I do.
What’s wrong with you?

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:39.990
You’re such a pain,
whining over a little prank...

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.580
Let’s hurry up
and keep going!

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:48.040
Ugh...
What’s wrong with me?!

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.680
Huh? What’s this?

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:03.090
You’re kidding me...
What’s wrong with this train?

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:04.710
You’re not scared again,
are you?

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.900
Bleh! Scaredy-cat!
Scaredy-cat!

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.670
Hey, me!
Stop being so mean!

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:11.530
I’m not scared!

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.880
Then you go first.

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:14.780
Umm...

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:17.290
Or how about some nice and fair
rock-paper-scissors to decide?

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:19.290
Oh, that’s more like it!

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:22.170
Okay, I accept.

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:24.040
So, you ready?

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:26.050
One match
crowns the winner!

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:29.900
Rock, paper... scissors!

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:34.790
Yay! I won!

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:37.010
You threw your hand late!

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:38.650
What are you talking about?

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:40.980
Got any proof?

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:43.900
C’mon, me!
Cheating is wrong!

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:47.070
Sorry...
I’m really sorry, Go!

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:59.750
What a creepy place...

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:02.620
Oh! Isn’t that
a will-o’-the-wisp?

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:04.280
A will-o’-the-wisp?!

00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:11.140
Oh, it was just a Yamirami?

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:17.800
Yamirami! Darkness Pokémon!
Evil/Ghost type!

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:20.220
It feeds on gemstone crystals!

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:24.850
Hey, Go! Look over here!
There’s zombies!

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.260
What are those things?

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:39.580
Tsuchinin! Trainee Pokémon!
Bug/Ground type!

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:42.170
It can live underground
for more than 10 years!

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:45.450
It absorbs nutrients
from the roots of trees!

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:51.510
Huh? They couldn’t be...

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:52.960
They evolved!

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:59.780
Tekkanin! Shinobi Pokémon!
Bug/Flying type!

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:03.940
It is so quick, it is said
to be able to avoid any attack!

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:05.760
Here they come!

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:06.340
Oh, no you don’t!

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:06.930
Satoshi?!

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:20.490
I’m going numb...

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:22.820
Pikachu... Thank you...

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:27.200
Nukenin’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:29.020
Huh? Added?

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:30.180
Why?

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:38.550
Nukenin! Shed Shell Pokémon!
Bug/Ghost type!

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:44.820
A most peculiar Pokémon that somehow appears
in a Monster Ball when a Tsuchinin evolves!

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:48.450
Hey, you!
When’d you get in his Ball?

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:50.280
Hey! Hey!

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:51.220
Come on, stop that, Satoshi.

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:52.020
You’re no fun!

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:58.820
Oh, it’s him!

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:00.570
Why...?

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:02.530
Why are humans
on the ghost train?

00:12:30.170 --> 00:12:31.380
What was that?

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:35.890
The luxury coach...

00:12:38.680 --> 00:12:39.960
But that’s...

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:49.090
Mikaruge...
It woke up...

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:55.050
Mikaruge! Sealed Pokémon!
Ghost/Evil type!

00:12:55.050 --> 00:12:58.090
A Pokémon
that was formed by 108 spirits!

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:01.090
There are some
ill-natured spirits in the mix!

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:03.600
Ill-natured spirits?

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:10.670
It says, “Return the spirit”...

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:12.600
You can understand
what Mikaruge says?!

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:15.330
Kind of...

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:18.360
But more to the point...
That boy...

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:24.700
Mikaruge!

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:27.020
What happened, Satoshi?!

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:31.200
Inside him... there is an ill-natured spirit
that Mikaruge once housed...

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:33.420
How did that happen?!

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:38.490
Oh! Is that why Satoshi’s
been acting so odd?

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:38.490
Mikaruge...

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:52.020
Mikaruge!

00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:56.530
Pull yourself together,
Satoshi!

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:58.530
How can we get him
back to normal?

00:13:58.530 --> 00:14:00.900
If you know how,
I need you to tell me!

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.240
Well...

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:07.600
Mika!

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:22.600
The Fuwante...

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:25.200
Hurry, everyone.

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:27.110
You’ll be a bit safer in here.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:32.160
This is bad...
That thing’s gonna derail the train.

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:35.100
If that happens,
everyone will...

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.360
I’ll stop Mikaruge!

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:42.110
So you have to
get Satoshi back to normal!

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:44.960
You know how,
don’t you?

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:47.160
But...

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:51.740
I’m Go. He’s Satoshi.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:55.620
I’m begging you!
He’s my precious friend!

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:01.260
I’ll try...

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:03.510
Thank you!

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:06.160
Monster Ball, go!

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:08.950
Let’s go, Absol!

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:14.520
Yabacha!

00:15:22.550 --> 00:15:24.480
May I ask you a favor?

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:33.910
Yabacha absorbs your life-force.

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:40.200
If this works, it may be able to flush
the ill-natured spirit out of Satoshi...

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:46.730
But Yabacha’s tea...

00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:47.930
...has a heinous taste.

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:51.870
Yuck!

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:56.620
Yuck, yuck, yuck, yuck,
yuck, yuck, <i>yuck!</i>

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:59.810
Mikaruge!
You need to calm down!

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:03.680
We’re trying to return you
your spirit as I speak!

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:05.850
So stop rampaging, and...

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:08.990
Crossroad Kill!

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:13.620
What did you do to me?!

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:17.500
U-Umm...
The spirit...

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:19.630
Huh?

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:22.240
It’ll be okay...
I know it will...

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:25.630
It’s coming out!

00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:36.960
Whoa...

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:38.390
Pikachu!

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:42.600
No!

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:44.110
That guy...!

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:47.420
Okay, if that’s what you want,
two can play at that game!

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:48.240
Come on out!

00:16:54.230 --> 00:16:56.870
Ooh... That’s a good choice.

00:16:57.300 --> 00:17:01.430
Gänger! Go and catch the guy
hiding in my shadow!

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:18.390
Okay, I’ll pull you back up!

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:31.150
Take that to Mikaruge.

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:33.350
Yeah, got it!

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:37.490
Dodge it!

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:51.090
This isn’t working...
It’s not giving me any openings...

00:17:57.060 --> 00:17:58.560
Dodge!

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:04.600
Absol!

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:12.880
Gänger?

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:15.620
Satoshi!

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:18.120
Yeah! It’s me, Satoshi!

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:20.910
Gänger’s got that guy’s spirit.

00:18:21.440 --> 00:18:22.530
I only need a moment.

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:24.960
Let’s stop it from moving!

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:27.220
I’ll use that opening
to give the spirit back!

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:28.190
Got it.

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:37.890
Good work, Gänger!

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:48.650
Absol!
Kick up some rubble!

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:55.140
Gänger! Now!

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:25.380
We did it!

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:05.140
They took it away.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:06.120
Is that okay?

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:07.730
Yeah.

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:11.770
Mikaruge wanted to go
to this graveyard.

00:20:11.770 --> 00:20:16.140
The Ghost Train
carries Ghost Pokémon.

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:20.040
Ghost Pokémon?
Nothing else?

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:23.920
Only me.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:49.080
That tired me out.

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:50.540
Sure was fun, though!

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:51.250
Maybe a little.

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:54.050
And we made it
to Lateral Town.

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:57.830
Geez, you always find a way
to look at the bright side.

00:21:02.450 --> 00:21:05.870
Oh, right!
I almost forgot.

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:07.110
Here’s your—

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:08.040
Huh?

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:09.780
Where’d...?

00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:11.710
The whole Ghost Train’s gone...

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:20.750
What’s going on here?

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:24.220
We really did
ride that thing, right?

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:31.730
The strange
and slightly scary Ghost Train...

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:39.990
Maybe someday you, too, might ride it
by mistake just as Satoshi and Go did.

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:09.610
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:11.120
Go!

00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:13.330
Let’s do our best, Gänger!

00:23:14.500 --> 00:23:17.290
If it drinks Dai Soup,
it can Kyodaimax.

00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:19.810
Oh, I think I’ve heard of that!

00:23:19.810 --> 00:23:24.680
If a Pokémon drinks Dai Soup
made from Dai Mushrooms, it can Kyodaimax!

00:23:24.680 --> 00:23:27.340
But... It won’t be easy.

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:29.440
Watch out, Satoshi!

00:23:29.440 --> 00:23:31.180
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:34.620
Gänger Goes All In!
The Road to Kyodaimax!!
